        <div id="mistakes" class="scroll-mt-24 mt-16">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-6">
            11. Common Mistakes to Avoid
          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Assuming every marshmallow powder is vegetarian</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                GHOST Lucky Charms and LGXNDS Charmies both list gelatin in their marshmallow pieces, and the GHOST pieces are colored partly with carmine, which comes from insects. If you avoid animal gelatin, choose a flavoring-only powder such as RYSE, Axe & Sledge or Pure Choice, and still read the panel on the tub you buy.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying the 20-serving RYSE tub</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                RYSE sells Jet-Puffed Marshmallow in 20, 27 and 54 serving sizes. The smallest costs the most per gram, while the 4 lb tub came to about $1.50 per 25 g at the price we saw. If you already know you like the flavor, the bigger tub saves real money over a year of shakes.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Trusting the Amazon title over the panel</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Listing titles are marketing copy. LGXNDS's Charmies title says 26 g of protein against 25 g on its panel, and the Axe & Sledge title says 1 g of sugar against 0 g. The supplement-facts panel is the legal label, so check it before you compare products or count macros.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Treating S'mores as a marshmallow flavor</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                S'mores powders from Optimum Nutrition, Nutricost, Legion and RYSE's Pop-Tarts line lean on chocolate and graham, with marshmallow as a background note. If what you want is the sweet vanilla marshmallow or the toasted campfire taste, pick a powder that names marshmallow as the main flavor instead.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Mixing it into boiling liquid</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Whey clumps and turns grainy in liquid that is too hot, and marshmallow pieces melt into a sticky film. For hot cocoa or coffee, let the drink cool below a simmer and whisk the powder in gradually, or blend it with a splash of cold milk first and then add the hot drink.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

